{"id":8987,"date":"2025-01-03T12:38:49","date_gmt":"2025-01-03T17:38:49","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=8987"},"modified":"2025-12-27T19:33:39","modified_gmt":"2025-12-28T00:33:39","slug":"freshen-up-the-rig","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2025\/01\/03\/freshen-up-the-rig\/","title":{"rendered":"Freshen Up the Rig"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>When we sold our motorhome last year, it was because we decided that we were going to live the lifestyle of Snobirds instead of RV Nomads.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We really enjoyed the six years or so we were traveling the country working in RV parks and government campgrounds.&nbsp; Not only did we travel extensively, but we met so many wonderful people along the way, many whom we are still friends with.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>But it made sense to sell our Airstream motorhome rather than have it sit here on our site in Arizona and let all that diesel motor muscle go to waste when some new owner could be having the thrill of driving her cross country.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It so happened that a neighbor of ours here at Rovers Roost in Arizona was going to move back home to Albuquerque and was offering her 5th wheel trailer for sale.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We jumped at the chance. It&#8217;s a 1996 Newmar American Star 30&#8242; 5th wheel trailer. Nearly 30 years old and not having been out of this park in the last 8 years, she shows her age a little, a lot more on the outside than inside.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>There&#8217;s the summer heat (up to about 115 deg) along with the intense cloudless sky, combined with daily winds blowing up the desert dust that had pretty much taken a toll on the old girl.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0852368593900636309647649.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8996\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0852368593900636309647649.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0852368593900636309647649-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0852368593900636309647649-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">1996 Newmar American Star 30&#8242; 5th wheel<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"225\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0852183222674175472518318-300x225.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8995\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0852183222674175472518318-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0852183222674175472518318-685x514.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0852183222674175472518318.jpg 720w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Faded and cracked decal graphics<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>But inside was good.&nbsp; Jimmy and Kathy were the original owners (We have the letter from Newmar welcoming them to the &#8220;family&#8221;) and since there was no smoking or children in the rig, it&#8217;s in pretty good shape.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We did get rid of the hide-a-bed couch and two recliners and replaced those with new furniture. We were able to get the carpet cleaned by a professional, replaced a couple light fixtures, and that&#8217;s about it for the interior.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The exterior however is a different story.&nbsp; The molding vinyl is the color of desert dirt, cracked and brittle.&nbsp; The caulk along the edges of the molding is dirty and the decal colored stripes are faded, cracked, and brittle.&nbsp; Trying to remove these old decals with a heat gun and plastic scraper is impossible.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"405\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_1130112122637263141107009.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8998\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_1130112122637263141107009.jpg 405w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_1130112122637263141107009-225x300.jpg 225w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 405px) 100vw, 405px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"225\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_113006897391844281891661-300x225.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8997\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_113006897391844281891661-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_113006897391844281891661-685x514.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_113006897391844281891661.jpg 720w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Old brittle trim molding<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0853265909357215140081808.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9001\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0853265909357215140081808.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0853265909357215140081808-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241129_0853265909357215140081808-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Cracked and faded decals. Note the desert dust stuck to the caulk around the windows<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>So to brighten things up I ordered a 100&#8242; roll of 5\/8&#8243; molding vinyl insert.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Using plastic scrapers from Harbor Freight along with paint thinner followed up with a Dawn Dish Soap solution, I was able to dissolve and scrape away most of the old butyl and\/or silicone caulk.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_1129185685470322023762281.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-8999\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_1129185685470322023762281.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_1129185685470322023762281-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241127_1129185685470322023762281-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">This shows the molding with old vinyl insert removed and new installed<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Although I tried to remove the decals, they were just too old and brittle, my only choice was to paint.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Kathy and I chose a color scheme that we think closely represents our southwest desert surroundings.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The dark brown bottom stripe represents the desert soil with the next stripe up referring to the blowing desert dust glowing a deep gold as the setting sun shines through.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The center deep green stripe reminds us of the various species of cactus that are everywhere around us while the bright orange strip shows off the beauty of the western setting sun with the brilliant blue stripe showing off the crystal clear cloudless Arizona sky that we can see for miles and miles.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241218_142702789372852136258940.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9003\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241218_142702789372852136258940.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241218_142702789372852136258940-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241218_142702789372852136258940-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"225\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241222_1520576911360934284898605-300x225.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9002\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241222_1520576911360934284898605-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241222_1520576911360934284898605-685x514.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241222_1520576911360934284898605.jpg 720w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"225\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241218_1426551156490015541170024-300x225.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-9004\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241218_1426551156490015541170024-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241218_1426551156490015541170024-685x514.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/20241218_1426551156490015541170024.jpg 720w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">As of this writing I still have the two top stripes (the ones that run through the window) to paint<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-video\"><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>When we sold our motorhome last year, it was because we decided that we were going to live the lifestyle of Snobirds instead of RV Nomads. We really enjoyed the six years or so we were traveling the country working in RV parks and government campgrounds.&nbsp; Not only did we travel extensively, but we met &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2025\/01\/03\/freshen-up-the-rig\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Freshen Up the Rig<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":9003,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[91,18285,264,554707999,554708025,554707823,30025],"tags":[554708215,554707508,554708216],"class_list":["post-8987","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-blogging","category-equipment","category-learning","category-repair","category-rving","category-technology","category-working","tag-newmar","tag-paint","tag-pin-striping"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8987","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=8987"}],"version-history":[{"count":7,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8987\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":9152,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/8987\/revisions\/9152"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/9003"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":